{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwyXVGYkdgjFy7ga4tG3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`vitest --repeats <number>` runs every test the given number of extra times, whether each run passes or fails. It's mainly for finding flaky tests: a test that passes once but fails on a later repeat shows itself. It's different from `--retry`, which only reruns tests that failed.\n\nIn the installed vitest 5.0.3, the default is `0`, so tests run once with no repeats. The runner loops from `0` to `repeats`, so `--repeats 3` runs each test 4 times in total. The CLI help describes it as \"Repeat every test a specific number of times regardless of the result.\" The same option can be set in the config file or on a single test. A Ludion note says it was added in vitest 5.0.0. I checked the behaviour against the installed package code."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":808,"cache_read_input_tokens":70762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":808},"output_tokens":241,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4dddda2-f94a-407d-b67c-100a1d7fb141","uuid":"18c0ac81-c048-44d6-9937-d70a810b0da1","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:48:49.816Z","request_id":"req_011CfwyXUvxXDPbWv6DHyTUv"}
